From 6dced9504e125ce67383c255b8a5d86c0ec1d536 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:56:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: replica freshness compares only primary-mode
 boards this home syncs; unpushed local changes keep the live row

Review t_01a1d3d80beee574 of 90194f5c59 (request_changes): lag_hold ignored the board's sync mode. In
`shadow` mode (`sync attach`'s default) the live board never applies the feed, so its cursor never moves
and the feed lag grows without bound; on a board detached to `off`, or one this home's config no longer
syncs, the replica stays on disk while pulls stop, so its pull stamp only ages. Either way sweep()
deferred every chat_wait_unclaimed notice until its episode expired, breaking the fail-open contract.

- kanban_replica_freshness._live_state: compare only when kanban_db_sync.board_mode(conn) == "primary"
  (it already folds in kanban.sync.enabled, kanban.sync.boards and a detach to off). Covers lag_hold
  and newer_rows alike.
- newer_rows: a card with a pending outbox op (an unpushed local change) is absent, so the relabel in
  _live_task keeps the live status rather than a replica row that predates the local change (nit 2).
- sweep(): the first deferred sweep of a lag stall logs at WARNING (later ones INFO), and the docstring
  says a deferral longer than MAX_EPISODE_SECONDS drops that episode's notice (nit 1).

Tests: the `synced` fixture now runs in primary mode with a drained outbox; new shadow-mode and
detached/disabled cases (test_kanban_ready_wait_checkpoint.py, 25 -> 28) and an unpushed-local-change
relabel case (test_kanban_wake_fold.py, 22 -> 23). Mutant without the primary gate fails the shadow,
detached and disabled cases; mutant without the outbox filter fails the unpushed case.
